# AIQE Playwright Harness

Application-agnostic AI harness for Playwright automation.
QA supplies flows under `inputs/`; generated code lives under `playwright-automation-framework/`.

## Workflow (always follow this order)

### Phase 1 — live-execution (mandatory before any code generation)
- Open a real browser via MCP Playwright (`@playwright/mcp`)
- At each new route or modal: capture screen map (DOM snapshot) BEFORE clicking
- Output: `playwright-automation-framework/support/screen-maps/<feature>.screen.json`
- Read full instructions: `skills/live-execution/SKILL.md`

### Phase 2 — automation-framework (POM generation)
- Read the screen map from Phase 1
- Generate: `pages/<feature>.page.ts`, `flows/<feature>.flow.ts`, `tests/e2e/<feature>.spec.ts`
- Every selector MUST use `getSelector(map, intent)` — no inline CSS, no guessing
- Read full instructions: `skills/automation-framework/SKILL.md`

### Phase 3 — test-healer (if tests fail)
- Classify error: timeout / selector not found / navigation / env
- Apply ONE fix per attempt: update selector from screen map, add `waitFor`, narrow scope
- Max 3 attempts — if still failing, report blocker and request screen map recapture
- Read full instructions: `skills/test-healer/SKILL.md`

## Entry point

For any request about automation, harness engineering, or Playwright:
**Start with `skills/pipeline-orchestrator/SKILL.md`**

